      "side": 1,
      "message": "Missing Matrix Mutation Triggers:\nHooking into individual property setters (`setRotation`, `setTranslationX`, `setScaleX`, etc.) misses several other ways a View\u0027s transform or visible bounds can change without a layout pass:\n1. `setPivotX(float)` / `setPivotY(float)` / `resetPivot()`: Changing the pivot alters the transformation matrix if rotation or scale is non-default.\n2. `setAnimationMatrix(@Nullable Matrix matrix)`: Extensively used by transition frameworks (such as `ChangeTransform` and `Transition`).\n3. `setCameraDistance(float)`: Affects 3D rotation perspective projections.\n4. `offsetLeftAndRight(int)` / `offsetTopAndBottom(int)`: Modifies bounds without a layout pass.\n5. `setElevation(float)`: Affects `getZ()` and the resulting shadow offset calculation in `gatherTransparentRegion()`.\n6. RenderThread-driven animations (`RenderNodeAnimator`): Property updates occurring directly on the RenderThread do not invoke Java property setters, so `notifyMatrixTransformChanged()` will not be triggered per frame.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "revId": "367516a95758494a892c38d3597c7b9f8aac501e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
