      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T11:41:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Covered in this patch (notifyMatrixTransformChanged() added)\n\nsetPivotX / setPivotY / resetPivot: When rotation/scale is non-default, pivot changes getMatrix(), so we now notify. With an identity matrix the region is unchanged and equals(mPreviousTransparentRegion) drops the no-op.\nsetCameraDistance: With non-zero rotationX/Y this dirties the 3D camera and the AABB, so we notify. With no 3D rotation the matrix is unchanged and equals drops the update.\noffsetLeftAndRight / offsetTopAndBottom: These mutate mLeft/mTop without a layout pass, and getGlobalVisibleRect maps from those fields. They invalidate and trigger a draw, but didLayout is false, so the dirty bit is required. We now notify.\nNot covered (intentional)\n\nsetAnimationMatrix: The animation matrix is a separate channel from the property transform. At draw time native code does concat(animationMatrix) then concat(transformMatrix). View.getMatrix() and gatherTransparentRegion → getGlobalVisibleRect only see the transform matrix, not the animation matrix. Hooking the setter would recompute from the un-transitioned layout bounds (same stale region) and add a gather on every ChangeTransform frame. View.draw() (legacy startAnimation()) and GhostView also write RenderNode.setAnimationMatrix and bypass the View setter. Covering this properly means mapRect of getAnimationMatrix() inside gather, which is outside this “sync the hint with property animation” change. The public JavaDoc on View.setAnimationMatrix() also tells app developers to use setRotation / setScaleX / setTranslationX instead.\nsetElevation: This only changes shadowOffset \u003d (int) getZ() in gatherTransparentRegion (a few pixels of shadow outset). It does not move the SurfaceView punch-through hole. The bug is hole desync during bound-changing animation. setTranslationZ already notifies.\nRenderNodeAnimator / ViewPropertyAnimator: These never call the Java setters. ObjectAnimator.ofFloat(view, View.TRANSLATION_X, …) does call View.setTranslationX() and is covered. view.animate() writes renderNode.setTranslationX() from onAnimationUpdate; RenderNodeAnimator updates native properties on RenderThread with no Java per-frame callback. This patch can only sync with UI-thread traversal. Covering ViewPropertyAnimator would need a notify in onAnimationUpdate, as a follow-up.\nThis change notifies every Java setter that updates getMatrix() or mLeft/mTop. RenderThread and animation-matrix paths need a separate follow-up.",
      "parentUuid": "cde4e8c8_e1e0f8e8",
      "revId": "367516a95758494a892c38d3597c7b9f8aac501e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
