      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T11:41:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the review. We agree with the geometry analysis. We are keeping getGlobalVisibleRect() on purpose, and the SurfaceView punch-through path is out of scope for this patch.\n\nAxis-aligned box vs rotated geometry\n\ngetGlobalVisibleRect() → getChildVisibleRect() uses getMatrix().mapRect(), so a non-orthogonal rotation yields an axis-aligned box strictly larger than the view. Region.Op.DIFFERENCE then subtracts that whole box, including the empty corners.\n\nWe still use that box because:\n\nandroid.graphics.Region is a union of axis-aligned rects. A true rotated polygon would have to be rasterized into the Region every animated frame, which is too expensive for this path.\nThe transparent region is only a SurfaceFlinger composition hint, not a clip. A larger box means “mark a bit more as opaque / composite a bit more,” which is safer than leaving the hint at the pre-animation position. With software composition and blending, empty-corner pixels with alpha 0 still show what is below.\nThe old logic used getLocationInWindow() plus untransformed width/height, so even the position was wrong under rotation/translation. The axis-aligned box at least tracks the transform, which is the bug this patch fixes.\nSome HWC paths may skip blending from the hint, so in an extreme case an empty corner could occlude what is below. That is a known precision limit of Region, not a regression from this change. Exact polygon coverage would be a separate change, outside “sync the hint with property animation.”\n\nSurfaceView punch-through\n\nAgreed: the SKIP_DRAW branch of SurfaceView.gatherTransparentRegion() still does UNION with getLocationInWindow() and getWidth()/getHeight(). Translation moves the top-left; rotation/scale do not change the hole’s shape.\n\nThis patch updates the opaque region of regular Views (DIFFERENCE) so a neighboring view’s property animation does not leave a stale opaque rect over a SurfaceView hole. Making the hole follow a SurfaceView’s own rotate/scale is a different path (UNION in SurfaceView.gatherTransparentRegion()) and is a follow-up.",
      "parentUuid": "c4b35989_45daca9e",
      "revId": "367516a95758494a892c38d3597c7b9f8aac501e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
