      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T11:41:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are not reusing mTransaction, and we dropped the long-lived mTranslateRegionTransaction field.\n\nWhy we do not reuse mTransaction\nmTransaction is a shared scratch object for the whole performTraversals, not a hint-only transaction.\n\n1.Later in the same traversal we call notifySurfaceCreated/Replaced(mTransaction) and applyTransactionOnDraw(mTransaction) again. Putting the hint on mTransaction first races those surface callbacks on the same object. If we take the immediate apply() path and it does not clear, hint ops can also be stacked with later ops and applied twice.\n2.Earlier in the same traversal mTransaction may already hold unapplied ops (crop, opaque, frame rate, etc.). applyTransactionOnDraw(mTransaction) at transparent-region time would flush those ops at the wrong moment.\n3.A long-lived hint transaction (mTranslateRegionTransaction in the original message) is also unsafe: applyTransactionOnDraw merges/holds the object we pass in. Clearing or mutating that same instance on the next frame races the pending merge.\n\nSo we allocate a short-lived transaction that only contains setTransparentRegionHint and hand it to applyTransactionOnDraw. equals(mPreviousTransparentRegion) means we only allocate when the region actually changes. The commit message now describes this; it no longer mentions mTranslateRegionTransaction.",
      "parentUuid": "030c215f_b8e6f4d5",
      "revId": "367516a95758494a892c38d3597c7b9f8aac501e",
